          "question": "Brought up something that looked like old coffee grounds this morning after a night of retching.",
          "answer": "**This needs emergency evaluation now, not later.** Call emergency services or go to the nearest emergency department today, even if you feel fine. The gastrointestinal bleeding guidance lists \"vomit that looks like coffee grounds\" under \"Call emergency services immediately\" (source: *Gastrointestinal bleeding*, gastroenterology and emergency medicine society guidance). Our automated risk check returned a \"routine\" tier because its fixed table did not match this wording. That tier is not a clearance, and I am overriding it on urgency because the guidance above is explicit.\n\nThe retrieved passages do not mention Mallory-Weiss tears, so I cannot confirm from them that retching caused this. Blood from forceful retching is one possibility a clinician would want to rule out. Bleeding from the upper digestive tract is another, and it is the reason for same-day emergency assessment. Only a clinician can tell the difference.\n\n**Call emergency services immediately, or go to the emergency department now, if you have any of these:**\n- Dizziness, light-headedness, or feeling faint or about to collapse\n- Fainting or collapse\n- Black, tarry, foul-smelling stools\n- Fast or pounding heartbeat\n- Cold, clammy, or pale skin\n- Confusion\n- Shortness of breath\n- Weakness that is new or getting worse\n- Severe or worsening abdominal pain\n\nDo not drive yourself if you feel faint. Ask someone to take you, or call for an ambulance. If you have any of these symptoms now, do not wait for a same-day appointment.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
